[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":53},"en/routes/conteudo-do-cubo.tsx",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10,"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":20,"_21":22,"_23":24,"_25":26,"_27":28},"tipo","etapa","cubo",{"_11":51,"_13":51,"_38":52},"id","basico-cruz","nome","White cross","rascunho",false,"html","<p>With the daisy done, each petal goes down to its place and forms the white <a href=\"/en/glossary#cruz\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"The 4 edges of one face (usually white) in place, lined up with the centers. The first step of the beginner method and of CFOP.\">cross</a> on the bottom. The cube stays with yellow on top.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;cross&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/377914973610cf0f.svg\" alt=\"The goal: the white cross on the bottom, each edge with its other color matching the center beside it.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The goal: the white cross on the bottom, each edge with its other color matching the center beside it.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;z2&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;cross&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/38da3c7a9a5d20d1.svg\" alt=\"The same cube, turned upside down (`z2`): the white cross in view.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>The same cube, turned upside down (<code>z2</code>): the white cross in view.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<h2>Line up and bring down</h2>\n<p>Each petal has another color besides white, facing the side. For each one:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Turn the top (<code>U</code>) until that color is above the center of the same color. For example: the green petal above the green center.</li>\n<li>Turn that face twice. If it is in front, <code>F2</code>. The petal goes down, with white facing down.</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama tira\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;F2&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;F2&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;cross&quot;}\"><ol aria-label=\"F2\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/825fcb3d54012c4c-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>F2</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/825fcb3d54012c4c-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>Petal lined up with the green in front: <code>F2</code>.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"diagrama tira\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;F2 U'&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;U F2&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;cross&quot;}\"><ol aria-label=\"U F2\"><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/07f3dbbd0671375e-0.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>U</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/07f3dbbd0671375e-1.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"><span class=\"giro\"><code>F2</code><span aria-hidden=\"true\">→</span></span></li><li><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/07f3dbbd0671375e-2.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"96\" height=\"96\" loading=\"lazy\"></li></ol><figcaption>Not lined up: the green petal is above orange. <code>U</code> takes it to green, and <code>F2</code> brings it down.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<p>Do the same with the other 3 petals. To work on a petal that is on another side, turn the whole cube around the yellow, without moving anything (the <code>y</code> <a href=\"/en/glossary#rotacao\" class=\"termo-do-glossario\" title=\"Turning the whole cube (x, y, z), without moving the pieces relative to each other.\">rotation</a>, in the <a href=\"/en/3x3/notation\">notation</a>): the face with the lined-up petal becomes the front, and yellow stays on top.</p>\n<h2>Check</h2>\n<p>Turn the cube over and look at the white face. The cross has to be complete, and each edge has to match the center beside it (green with green, red with red). If an edge is swapped, take it back to the daisy and bring it down again.</p>\n<div class=\"diagramas\"><figure class=\"diagrama\" data-cubo=\"{&quot;cubo&quot;:&quot;3x3&quot;,&quot;embaralhar&quot;:&quot;z2&quot;,&quot;tira&quot;:&quot;&quot;,&quot;modo&quot;:&quot;cross&quot;}\"><img src=\"/imagens/diagramas/f2a1c83ca5b54dfd.svg\" alt=\"Right cross: white in the middle, and each edge with the color of the center beside it.\" width=\"140\" height=\"140\" loading=\"lazy\"><figcaption>Right cross: white in the middle, and each edge with the color of the center beside it.</figcaption></figure></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Tip:</strong> don&#39;t skip lining up. If the petal goes down in the wrong place, the cross ends up with swapped colors and the next step won&#39;t work.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>If you already make the cross directly, without the daisy, you can use the cards of this step: they show the two most common cases.</p>\n","treino","/3x3/treino?grupo=basico/cruz/casos","metodos",[46],"anterior",{"_13":44,"_38":45},"proximo",{"_13":42,"_38":43},"grupos",[29],{"_11":30,"_13":14,"_31":32,"_33":34,"_35":16,"_36":37,"_38":39},"Passo 1","nivel","iniciante","casos",2,"conjunto","ids",[40,41],"endereco","/3x3/basico/cruz/casos","B1-Branco-em-cima","B1-Branco-na-frente","1st layer","/3x3/basico/primeira-camada","The daisy","/3x3/basico/flor",{"_13":47,"_48":49,"_38":50},"Beginner method","numero",3,"/3x3/basico#cruz","3x3","/3x3/",{"_54":55,"_56":57},"cubos",[60,61,62,63,64,65],"idiomas",[58,59],"pt","en",{"_11":51,"_13":51},{"_11":72,"_13":72},{"_11":71,"_13":71},{"_11":70,"_13":70},{"_11":68,"_13":69},{"_11":66,"_13":67},"pyraminx","Pyraminx","megaminx","Megaminx","5x5","4x4","2x2"]
